Kanna includes code derived from the following projects.

================================================================================
kmux
https://github.com/tampopogk/kmux
MIT License, at kmux 6a022cb unless noted otherwise.
references/kmux is kmux itself at 13c78f4 (a git subtree, under its own
LICENSE and NOTICE), kept as the reference model's source and tests; it is
not built into Kanna.
================================================================================

Derived from kmux:

  crates/kanna-mux
      A Rust port of kmux's core, apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxCore (Core.swift,
      Core+Layout.swift, Model.swift, JSON.swift, Fraction.swift, Brand.swift,
      Instance.swift, SocketServer.swift), and of its reference model,
      reference/kmux/core.js and reference/kmux/index.html. Its layout
      owner (src/owner.rs) keeps and saves the layout by kmux's rules in
      apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/AppController.swift (restoreLayout,
      scheduleSave, saveLayout): a file it can't trust is set aside as
      .bad, and a save that would change nothing writes nothing.

  crates/kanna-layout
      kanna-mux's layout owner for Kanna.app, behind a C interface.

  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/AppController.swift
      Parts follow apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/AppController.swift: --bg and
      `present`, the socket and signal handling, one WindowController per
      window kept in step with the layout (sync, makeController), and
      saving the layout half a second after a change and on quit
      (scheduleSave), with --fresh.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Control/Commands.swift
      The request envelope and error follow Core.handle and KmuxError in
      apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxCore/Core.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Control/JSON.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxCore/JSON.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Control/SocketServer.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxCore/SocketServer.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Snapshot.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Snapshot.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/SyntheticKey.swift
      From SyntheticKey in apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Shortcuts.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/main.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/main.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Terminal/GhosttyRuntime.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Terminal/GhosttyRuntime.swift, with the
      options and attach split of kmux's spike/ghostty-external-io branch.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Terminal/TerminalSurfaceView.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Terminal/TerminalSurfaceView.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Terminal/ExternalIO.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Terminal/TerminalBackend.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Terminal/ExternalIO.swift and
      TerminalBackend.swift on kmux's spike/ghostty-external-io branch.

  From kmux 1f05ccb, with comments removed:
  apps/kanna/Sources/KannaDiagram
      From apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxDiagram; merman's module is KannaMerman.
      At kmux 39abfb9, with class diagrams and git graphs.
  apps/kanna/Sources/KannaMarkdown
      From apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxMarkdown; its attributes are kanna.*.
  apps/kanna/Sources/SimBridge
      From apps/kmux/Sources/SimBridge.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Panes/WebPaneView.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/WebPaneView.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Panes/IosPaneView.swift
      From apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/IosPaneView.swift; Simulator.reattach is
      Kanna's.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Panes/Contents.swift
      Starting, stopping and reporting web, markdown and iOS panes
      follow ContentHost in apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/ContentHost.swift; the
      debug.web, debug.md and debug.ios commands in Debug.swift follow
      apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/AppController.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/WindowController.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/TabBar.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/PaneView.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/Dragging.swift
      From the same files in apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux, drawing the layout
      model's view (JSON) instead of KmuxCore's Model.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/Shortcuts.swift
      Shortcut from apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Shortcuts.swift.
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/Menus.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/Moving.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Windows/PaneViews.swift
  apps/kanna/Sources/Kanna/Debug.swift
      The menus, actions, Ghostty actions, dragging (pane and tab drops,
      debug.drag), the pane views' registry and the debug commands
      (debug.key, debug.click, debug.menu, debug.pinch, debug.stats)
      follow apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/AppController.swift and ContentHost.swift.
      The docked pane (the window split into it and the tabs' side, its
      divider, DockDividerView, Show Tab ⌘1–⌘9, ⌘W doing nothing in it)
      follows kmux a759abd.
  crates/kanna-mux/src/owner.rs, src/model.rs
      The focused call follows AppController.focused, and divider follows
      DividerView in apps/kmux/Sources/Kmux/Dragging.swift. The docked
      pane follows apps/kmux/Sources/KmuxCore (Model.swift, Core.swift,
      Core+Layout.swift, State.swift) at a759abd.
  crates/kanna/src/commands.rs, crates/kanna/src/output.rs and
  crates/kanna/src/lib.rs
      A port of kmux's CLI, crates/kmux/src/commands.rs, output.rs and
      main.rs (the command table, parsing, help, `commands --json`,
      `instances`, `raw`, errors and output), branded kanna, with Kanna's
      additions (read, --mux, --, exit 6, Kanna's instances). Docked
      panes (open --dock, move --dock and --tab, the dock line in list)
      are from kmux a759abd.
      crates/kanna/tests/kmux_reference.rs compiles kmux's commands.rs
      and output.rs, unchanged, to check the port against them.
  crates/kanna-client
      From kmux's crates/kmux-client at 1f05ccb (the control-socket
      client, exit codes and argument reader), with Args.optional from
      a759abd, comments removed.
  crates/kanna-merman
      From kmux's crates/kmux-merman at 1f05ccb (the C bridge to merman),
      comments removed, its symbols renamed kanna_merman_*; linked
      into the app by crates/kanna-ffi rather than its own library.

  scripts/env.sh                 follows kmux's scripts/env.sh
  scripts/build-ghosttykit.sh    follows kmux's scripts/build-ghosttykit.sh
  scripts/build-kanna-app.sh     follows kmux's scripts/build-kmux.sh

